<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" effectiveDate="2026-07-15">
  <p>
    This policy explains how Kyter, LLC handles information when you use Simalytics. Simalytics
    is an independent companion for Simkl and requires a Simkl account for its core features.
  </p>

  <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Simalytics stores your Simkl access token in the iOS Keychain. Synced watchlists, viewing
    progress, ratings, memos, title metadata, preferences, and image caches are stored locally on
    your device so the app can load quickly and work reliably.
  </p>
  <p>
    Signing out removes the Simkl access token and locally synced library data. Uninstalling the
    app removes its local data according to iOS behavior.
  </p>

  <h2>Simkl account data</h2>
  <p>
    Sign-in occurs on Simkl's website. Simalytics receives an authorization code and exchanges it
    for a Simkl access token through Kyter's API. The app does not request your name or email
    address from Simkl.
  </p>
  <p>
    Simalytics sends the access token to Simkl to retrieve and update information in your Simkl
    account. This includes your account identifier, watchlists, viewing progress, ratings, memos,
    and related title activity. Simkl links this information to your Simkl account and handles it
    under its own privacy policy and account settings. Simalytics also sends search terms to
    Simkl's public search API without attaching your Simkl access token.
  </p>

  <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
  <p>
    Simalytics uses Sentry to receive crash reports, performance measurements, and other technical
    diagnostics used to maintain app functionality. Simalytics does not attach your name, email
    address, or Simkl profile to Sentry events. Authorization, token, and cookie headers are
    redacted before events are sent. This diagnostic information is not used for advertising or
    tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>Kyter API and infrastructure</h2>
  <p>
    Kyter's Cloudflare Worker exchanges the Simkl authorization code, validates Simkl access
    tokens, and proxies selected TMDB requests. It has no application database and does not
    intentionally persist authorization codes or access tokens. Cloudflare processes request
    metadata and operational logs needed to deliver, secure, and monitor the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Other services</h2>
  <p>Simalytics uses the following services to provide app functionality:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://simkl.com/privacy-tos/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Simkl</a>
      for account sign-in, library synchronization, searches, and title data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sentry</a>
      for crash, performance, and diagnostic reporting.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Cloudflare</a
      > for API hosting, security, and operational observability.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >TMDB</a
      > for cast, person, and watch-provider information.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Photos, location, advertising, and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Simalytics can add a poster to your photo library only when you choose Save Image. It does not
    read or upload your photo library. Simalytics does not collect precise location, contacts, or
    advertising identifiers, and it does not use data for third-party advertising or cross-app
    tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>Support communications</h2>
  <p>
    The Send Feedback action opens your email app. Kyter receives your email address and anything
    you choose to include only if you send that message. Support correspondence is retained only
    as needed to respond, maintain appropriate business records, and comply with legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Data in your Simkl account is retained and deleted according to Simkl's policies and controls.
    You can sign out to remove Simalytics' local account data, manage or delete your Simkl account
    through Simkl, and uninstall Simalytics to remove its local data. Diagnostic and infrastructure
    records are retained according to Sentry's and Cloudflare's configured service policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    To ask Kyter about its data or request deletion of support correspondence, email
    <a href="mailto:dev@kyter.com">dev@kyter.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Simalytics is not directed to children under 13, and Kyter does not knowingly collect personal
    information from children under 13 through the app. Contact
    <a href="mailto:dev@kyter.com">dev@kyter.com</a> if you believe a child has provided personal
    information to Kyter.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Kyter uses reasonable technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the information
    it processes. No transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Kyter may update this policy when Simalytics or its service providers change. The effective
    date at the top of this page identifies the latest revision.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:dev@kyter.com">dev@kyter.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
